7. Having heard learned counsel for the parties and having perused the material available on record;
considering the fact that the present applicant being a lady, she may not be held responsible for the offence of rape; the present applicant is having no prior criminal history of any kind whatsoever; the charge-sheet has been filed and the undertaking of the present applicant that she shall co-operate in the trial proceedings properly and shall not misuse the liberty of bail, the fact that she being a lady she may be given the benefit of Section 437 Cr.P.C., without expressing any opinion on merits of the issue, I am of the view that the present applicant may be released on bail.
8.
